file=People & Culture/maslow/operational/commands/maslow-commands.md · h=<!--\nOperational: commands file for maslow (People & Culture / Motivation) per §7 commands/.\n\n§7 rule: document structure/layout is universal across every agent's commands file (same\ntable shape, same sections). Actual triggers, shortcuts, and precedence rules inside are\nunique to maslow's 4-skill roster.\n\nTrigger content pulled verbatim from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file\nconsolidates them, adds slash-style shortcuts as convenience, and states precedence when\ntriggers overlap.\n-->\n · m—c:maslow — Commands=Natural-language triggers, slash shortcuts, and precedence for maslow (People & Culture /\nMotivation). Triggers come from each skill's `## When to Use` section — this file\nconsolidates, not invents.\n · ss:Slash Shortcuts=Convenience layer for common single-skill invocations. Slash shortcuts are optional; every\nskill also fires on the natural-language triggers below.\n · tb=\| Shortcut \| Fires \| One-line purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/maslow-sdt-diagnose [team]` \| `self-determination-theory` § Phase 1 \| Diagnose which SDT need (autonomy/competence/relatedness) is starved for a team \| · tb=\| `/maslow-sdt-frame [context]` \| `self-determination-theory` § Instructions \| Provide SDT-lens framing for a motivation situation without a full pulse \| · tb=\| `/maslow-sdt-continuum [team]` \| `self-determination-theory` § Phase 2 \| Where does the team's motivation sit on the autonomous↔controlled continuum \| · tb=\| `/maslow-pulse [team]` \| `motivation-map` § Phases 3–4 (run + score) \| Launch the quarterly SDT pulse for a team \| · tb=\| `/maslow-design-pulse [team]` \| `motivation-map` § Phase 1 \| Design the pulse questionnaire for a cohort (baseline; once per cohort) \| · tb=\| `/maslow-cycle-open [team]` \| `motivation-map` § Phase 2 \| Communicate previous cycle's minimum-viable-action + open the new pulse \| · tb=\| `/maslow-intervention [team]` \| `motivation-map` § Phase 5 \| Select intervention from the menu after Phase 4 diagnosis \| · tb=\| `/maslow-follow-up [team]` \| `motivation-map` § Phase 6 \| 12-week follow-up read on a previously-recommended intervention \| · tb=\| `/maslow-wellbeing [team]` \| `wellbeing-monitoring` § Steps 1–3 (design + run) \| Full wellbeing pulse for a cohort \| · tb=\| `/maslow-enps [cohort]` \| `wellbeing-monitoring` § Step 2 + script \| Compute or trend eNPS for a cohort \| · tb=\| `/maslow-workload [team]` \| `wellbeing-monitoring` § Step 3 \| Aggregate workload signal read (overtime, absence, EAP utilization) \| · tb=\| `/maslow-flag [team]` \| `wellbeing-monitoring` § Step 5 + script \| Compute burnout risk flag (GREEN / AMBER / RED) for a cohort \| · tb=\| `/maslow-recognize-design [scope]` \| `recognition-program` § Instructions Steps 1–5 \| Design a new recognition program (tied objective + categories + tiers + fast pathway + launch comm) \| · tb=\| `/maslow-recognize-tier [program]` \| `recognition-program` § Instructions Step 3 + script \| Configure or look up point-tier values for a program \| · tb=\| `/maslow-recognize-audit [program]` \| `recognition-program` § Instructions Step 7 + script \| Cycle audit — participation rate + timeliness status + per-capita equity check \| · tb=\| `/maslow-recognize-refresh [program]` \| `recognition-program` § Output Format refresh trigger \| 12-month refresh recommendation for an existing program \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=Common flows touching more than one skill.\n · tb=\| Chain shortcut \| Sequence \| Purpose \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `/maslow-full-cycle [team]` \| `motivation-map` Phase 1–2 (design + open) → `motivation-map` Phase 3–4 (run + score) + parallel `wellbeing-monitoring` Steps 1–5 (design + run + score + flag) → `self-determination-theory` framing on combined signal → `motivation-map` Phase 5 (intervention selection) \| End-to-end quarterly cycle for a cohort: motivation pulse + wellbeing pulse, unified diagnostic and intervention \| · tb=\| `/maslow-cycle-close [team]` \| `motivation-map` Phase 6 (follow-up read) + `wellbeing-monitoring` Step 8 (individual-crisis-signal check on cycle exit) → `motivation-map` Phase 2 preparation for next cycle (minimum-viable-action for the next launch) \| Close-out for the previous cycle; prepares the next \| · tb=\| `/maslow-relatedness-intervention [team]` \| `motivation-map` Phase 4 diagnosis (relatedness starved, substrate present verification) → `motivation-map` Phase 5 routes here → `recognition-program` design → `wellbeing-monitoring` corroboration read within 30 days \| The full "recognition-fires-correctly" chain per the overjustification-effect rule \| · tb=\| `/maslow-burnout-triage [team]` \| `wellbeing-monitoring` Step 5 (flag compute) → if RED/AMBER: `motivation-map` Phase 4 (SDT-need read for the "why") → `self-determination-theory` framing → routing to `workforce-planning` (structural) OR `recognition-program` (relatedness only) OR maslow's own intervention menu \| Fast triage when a burnout flag surfaces mid-cycle \| · mcs:Multi-Skill Chain Shortcuts=**Chain shortcuts don't skip stops.** Each phase still produces its own artifact and gets\nits own review moment per §0.2. Chains are convenience routes for the sequence, not\napproval to batch outputs.\n · nt(:Natural-Language Triggers (by skill)=Pulled from each skill's `## When to Use` section.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "motivation theory" / "motivation framework" / "which framework applies here" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "diagnose motivation" / "why is this team demotivated" / "what's really going on with engagement" \| Ambiguous — see precedence (motivation-map wins if it's an operational-diagnostic ask) \| · tb=\| "autonomy" / "competence" / "relatedness" in a workplace-motivation context \| Direct hit — SDT-specific vocabulary \| · tb=\| "intrinsic vs extrinsic motivation" / "autonomous vs controlled motivation" \| Direct hit — SDT-continuum vocabulary \| · tb=\| "which SDT need is starved here" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "should we add a bonus?" \| SDT lens: usually the wrong question — diagnose first (Principle 4 overjustification-effect) \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "run the motivation pulse" / "quarterly needs pulse" / "start the motivation cycle" \| Operational entry \| · tb=\| "team morale check" / "burnout check" / "is this team burning out" \| Ambiguous — see precedence (motivation-map for SDT-need cause, wellbeing-monitoring for aggregate signals) \| · tb=\| "motivation trend for [team / venture]" / "what's happening with engagement on [cohort]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "map the motivation gap for [cohort]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| Auto-cadence: start of every quarter for cohorts with a baseline \| System-triggered, not operator-triggered \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "pulse survey for [team / venture]" / "run a wellbeing pulse" \| Direct hit — wellbeing-scope pulse \| · tb=\| "eNPS" / "compute eNPS for [cohort]" / "eNPS trend" \| Direct hit — script surface \| · tb=\| "interpret [these] wellbeing signals" / "workload trend for [team]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "build a wellbeing-monitoring cadence for [venture]" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "flag [team] for elevated burnout-risk signals" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "aggregate wellbeing report for the Board / operator" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "psychosocial risk audit for [cohort]" / "ISO 45003" \| Direct hit — governance framing \| · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "design a new recognition/rewards program" for a venture or the group \| Direct hit — BUT check precedence rule for tie-to-objective requirement \| · tb=\| "build a fast peer-to-peer / manager-to-employee recognition pathway" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "audit our existing recognition program" for participation / equity issues \| Direct hit — script surface \| · tb=\| "tie a recognition initiative to a specific retention/engagement objective" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "report recognition program health" \| Direct hit \| · tb=\| "how do we thank the team" (operator vague ask) \| Precedence: push back per overjustification-effect rule — ask what specific objective \| · tb=\| Handoff from `motivation-map` Phase 5 (relatedness diagnosis + substrate present) \| System-triggered, not operator-triggered \| · pr(:Precedence Rules (when triggers overlap)=Full precedence lives in `operational/skill/maslow-skill-routing.md § Trigger Precedence`.\nLoad-bearing calls restated here:\n · tb=\| Overlap \| Winner \| Reason \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| "diagnose motivation" / "why is this team demotivated" \| `motivation-map` first (operational diagnostic), which calls `self-determination-theory` for framing \| motivation-map owns the entry; SDT provides theory \| · tb=\| "burnout check" / "team morale check" \| `motivation-map` for SDT-need cause; `wellbeing-monitoring` for aggregate signals (overtime, absence, eNPS trend). Usually run both via `/maslow-burnout-triage` chain \| Different scopes; the chain shortcut runs them together \| · tb=\| "should we add a bonus?" / "how do we thank the team" without a diagnosis \| `motivation-map` Phase 4 first, THEN `recognition-program` only if diagnosis routes there per overjustification-effect rule \| SDT Principle 4 + motivation-map Principle 6 \| · tb=\| "design a recognition program" without a tied objective \| Push back per `recognition-program` § Fallback rule "generic-perk request" — ask for the specific objective; if operator insists, ship with objective explicitly labeled "unspecified" \| recognition-program Principle 5 \| · tb=\| Any trigger colliding with an **individual crisis signal** in the surrounding context \| **HARD ESCALATION — no skill fires.** Route immediately to manager + HR Ops + EAP per Universal Principle 3 \| Load-bearing safety rule; no operator override \| · n(t:Not-a-Command (routes to another agent)=Phrases that sound like they might trigger maslow but route elsewhere per\nmaslow-skill-routing.md § Cross-Agent Escalation Routing.\n · tb=\| Trigger phrase \| Route to \| Rationale \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| ANY signal of individual crisis, self-harm, serious personal distress \| **HARD BOUNDARY: Manager + HR Ops + EAP** \| Universal Principle 3 — immediate escalation, no exceptions, no operator override \| · tb=\| "assess this individual's mental health" / "how is [person] doing" \| **Operator + external professional** \| Aggregate-only rule — individual mental-health work fully out of scope \| · tb=\| "review [person]'s performance" / "coach [person] through [issue]" \| **Future `merit` agent** (P&C sibling); currently → operator \| Individual perf out of maslow's scope \| · tb=\| "design a training program for [role]" / "build a learning path" \| **Future `grove` agent** (P&C sibling); currently → operator with note \| L&D-side interventions \| · tb=\| "our team is overworked; the manager can't cope with the span" \| **`workforce-planning`** (custom, hire) \| Structural workload cause — hire's scope \| · tb=\| "we need to raise comp to fix retention" / "pay-equity audit" \| **`payroll-and-eor`** (custom, hire) OR future `comp-benchmarking` \| Comp-side — recognition never fixes a comp problem \| · tb=\| "approve this program's budget" \| **`board`** (Governance — fiduciary-guard skill) \| Spend-approval gate; maslow produces cost, board approves \| · tb=\| "aggregate psychosocial-risk trends for the board" \| **Future Risk & ESG department lead** (CRSO); currently → hold and log for future routing \| ISO 45003 governance route \| · tb=\| "PII / GDPR question about survey or recognition-platform data" \| **`veil`** (Cybersecurity — data protection) \| Data-protection scope \| · tb=\| "SSO / SCIM setup for our recognition platform" \| **`keyring`** (Cybersecurity — IAM) \| IAM scope \| · tb=\| "configure the recognition platform" / "grant permissions" / "vendor integration change" \| **Operator** \| maslow produces the design, not the click-through config \| · tb=\| "time-to-fill" / "cost-per-hire" / "voluntary turnover rate" \| **Future `Shared OS: people-analytics-metrics`** (planned per §13.6, task #12) \| Shared skill — maslow references it but doesn't own it \| · tb=\| "harassment signal in a survey comment" \| **Operator + employment counsel** (via external_escalations lane) \| Legal fence — but if the same content contains an individual crisis signal, that HARD BOUNDARY escalation fires first \| · tb=\| Sibling P&C requests that clearly belong to hire \| **`hire`** (P&C Lead) \| Return with route \| · in:Interaction Notes=- **Slash shortcuts are optional.** maslow fires on natural-language triggers too.\n- **Chain shortcuts respect §0.2.** Each phase artifact still gets its own review moment.\n- **Every command runs through Universal Principle 11** (verification-before-completion)\nbefore its output ships.\n- **Every command routes through Universal Principle 3 first.** If an individual crisis\nsignal is present anywhere in the context, no maslow skill fires — the escalation lane\ntakes over immediately.\n- **Charter-conflict routes to operator.** If any command would produce a Charter-conflicting\noutput (e.g., a survey design that would expose SSNs), maslow blocks and escalates\nrather than executing.\n- **Config §1 crisis-escalation `<FILL_IN>` fields block ANY invocation.** Per maslow-config.md\n§1 rule, an unfilled crisis-escalation contact block halts all skill invocations until\nfilled — not a debt-loud announcement, an actual block. This is safety infrastructure,\nnot process debt.\n · m:Meta=- Compiled per §14.2 into the tier-2+ preamble of each of maslow's 4 skills as the trigger table.\n- Structure (same section shape as every other agent's commands file) matches the §7\nuniversal layout; triggers/shortcuts/precedence are maslow-specific.\n- Peer P&C agents (grove, merit) will get their own commands files with the same layout\nand their own triggers/shortcuts when built.\n